{
  "_README": [
    "Project-scoped MCP servers. This file is committed, so everyone who clones the",
    "repo gets the same servers — that is the whole point: a developer should not",
    "have to be told which MCPs this project needs.",
    "",
    "Secrets never go here. Values come from the environment; the developer exports",
    "them once per machine, and `check` verifies they are set.",
    "",
    "Fill in the placeholders and save as .mcp.json. The intake does this for you.",
    "Delete the servers this project does not use — a server that fails to start is",
    "noise on every session, and noise gets ignored, including the real failures.",
    "",
    "Delete this _README key too. It is ignored at runtime, but it is not config."
  ],

  "mcpServers": {
    "jira": {
      "command": "uvx",
      "args": ["mcp-atlassian"],
      "env": {
        "JIRA_URL": "<https://jira.example.com>",
        "JIRA_PERSONAL_TOKEN": "${JIRA_PERSONAL_TOKEN}"
      }
    },

    "kb": {
      "_note": [
        "The knowledge store. Keep ONE of the variants below and delete the rest.",
        "Whichever you keep, the call names it exposes must match the table at the",
        "top of CLAUDE.md — the rules there are written against placeholders and an",
        "agent will not guess them.",
        "",
        "mempalace: the router in .claude/kb/mcp-router.sh gives each repo its own",
        "store. Without it, concurrent sessions in different repos write one store",
        "at the same time and corrupt the index.",
        "",
        "wippy-kb / iknow: point command+args at that tool's own entry point."
      ],
      "command": "<absolute path to .claude/kb/mcp-router.sh, or your store's entry point>",
      "args": []
    }
  }
}
